        "# Dunder\n",
        "\n",
        "“Dunder” means double underscore, commonly referring to names such as `__init__` that begin and end with two underscores. Many such names have special meaning to Python.\n",
        "\n",
        "Source: [Python glossary](https://docs.python.org/3/glossary.html#term-dunder)"
      ]
